   "id": "ca_asleep_at_the_wheel_2",
   "area_id": "ca_mt_chamberlin",
   "name": "Asleep at the Wheel",
   "grade": "5.12-",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "A long Sierra crack route up the central buttress. Pitch 0 scrambles filthy third-class ledges up to an alcove at the buttress's left end. Pitches 1 and 2 (5.11) work cracks, a finger corner and roof, then a hand traverse under a roof and a chimney. Pitch 3 (5.10) climbs thin cracks to the route's big corner facing right. Pitch 4 (5.11 PG13) has poor rock and a separated column. Pitch 5 (5.11 R) has sparse gear and runouts. Pitch 6 (5.10) is knobby; pitch 7 (5.12-) stems and chimneys to a roof. The upper pitches may be off route.",
