   "overview": "Eleven pitches, 5.7 to 5.11, up a giant dihedral on a buttress. Early-season snow can cover the scramble to the base. A slab holding a 5.7 RX stretch and one 5.9+ move connects to the corner. Within the upper corner come fist-to-finger jamming, then 5.11 overhangs, then a 5.9R offwidth (the biggest cam removes the R). After the 5th class, unrope and walk off right, skipping the final tower, whose rock looked poor.",
